1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,848
Every midnight, my future self calls my phone. He warns me about tiny mistakes before they ruin my upcoming day.

2
00:00:08,148 --> 00:00:16,236
He told me to avoid the freeway Tuesday, so I dodged a six-car pileup. He saved my life three times.

3
00:00:16,536 --> 00:00:27,720
Because of his constant warnings, my life became totally predictable, utterly safe, and completely hollow. I stopped taking any real risks.

4
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:36,420
Tonight, my phone rings right on schedule. But when I hit play, his voice isn't calm anymore—he's absolutely terrified.

5
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:43,776
He whispers, 'Do not answer the knock at your front door tonight. If you open it, everything we built shatters.'

6
00:00:44,076 --> 00:00:53,676
My heart hammers against my ribs. I freeze in the dark hallway as heavy, deliberate footsteps approach outside my apartment door.

7
00:00:53,976 --> 00:01:02,784
The sharp knock echoes through the silence. I stare at the brass peephole, holding my breath, terrified of what waits outside.

8
00:01:03,084 --> 00:01:11,844
I break my future self's golden rule and look through the glass. Standing in the dim corridor is a young woman holding flowers.

9
00:01:12,144 --> 00:01:21,768
I realize the truth: my future self wasn't protecting my life. He was a lonely old man protecting his own cowardice from love.

10
00:01:22,068 --> 00:01:28,572
I pull the door wide open and smile. Tonight, I finally stop listening to the voice on my phone.
